"""simple cash day: initial opening and direct close (FM-SIMPLE-CASH-010)

Revision ID: 0023
Revises: 0022
Create Date: 2026-10-13 09:00:00.000000

Additive over 0020-0022. A plain till: a new ``initial`` opening source (a declared amount, zero allowed, ONE
``opening_initial_fund`` movement, never a capital movement) and a direct ``open -> closed`` close for those sessions
(counted of any size, ``difference = counted - expected`` recorded as a difference, no denomination count, receiver or
handover). No row of 0020-0022 is rewritten, nothing is backfilled and Capital tables are untouched: ``zero`` / ``capital``
/ ``handover`` / ``legacy`` sessions keep exactly their contracts.

Downgrade is LOSSLESS ONLY: it REFUSES (before any change) when any ``initial`` session or ``opening_initial_fund``
movement exists, otherwise it removes the 0023 artifacts and restores the exact 0022 functions.
"""
